;; Which error was thrown, as one alphabet for both sides (docs/notes/fuzzing.md, "Errors").

;; A JVM throw is its class and message, ours its ex-type and message. Each side maps to a family by the first rule

;; that matches; the comparison is of families, so the same mistake reported in other words still agrees and a

;; different mistake does not. A throw no rule matches stays its raw text and diverges from everything, which is how

;; a new message asks to be classified.

;; Our runtime errors carry no ex-type (design §4 «Тип ошибки, `catch` по кейворду, отмена»: everything else is nil),

;; so ours are classified by message; an ex-type that is not nil is its own family.

{:families
 {:index "an index or a range outside its collection or string"
  :arith "integer overflow, or an integer divided by zero"
  :arity "a fn called with a count of arguments it has no arity for"
  :state "an operation the value's state refuses: `pop` of an empty vector"
  :argument "an argument of the right type with a value the operation refuses"
  :type "an argument of a type the operation does not take, nil included"}

 ;; [class-regex message-regex-or-nil family], first match wins.
 :jvm
 [["^java\\.lang\\.(String|Array)?IndexOutOfBoundsException$" nil :index]
  ["^java\\.lang\\.ArithmeticException$" nil :arith]
  ["^clojure\\.lang\\.ArityException$" nil :arity]
  ["^java\\.lang\\.IllegalStateException$" nil :state]
  ["^java\\.lang\\.IllegalArgumentException$" "^Don't know how to create ISeq from" :type]
  ["^java\\.lang\\.IllegalArgumentException$" "^(Key|Index) must be integer" :type]
  ["^java\\.lang\\.IllegalArgumentException$" "^bit operation not supported for" :type]
  ["^java\\.lang\\.(IllegalArgumentException|NumberFormatException)$" nil :argument]
  ["^java\\.lang\\.(ClassCastException|NullPointerException|UnsupportedOperationException)$" nil :type]]

 ;; [message-regex family], first match wins, for a throw whose ex-type is nil.
 :ours
 [["^Wrong number of args|takes \\d+ argument\\(s\\), got" :arity]
  ["out of bounds|(?i:index out of range)" :index]
  ["^Divide by zero$|overflow|^Non-terminating decimal expansion" :arith]
  ["^Can't pop empty" :state]
  ["^No value supplied for key|^Value out of range for|^Argument must be an integer|^Infinite or NaN$" :argument]
  ["cannot be cast|not supported on (this )?type|expects an? |Don't know how to create ISeq|cannot be invoked|is not a number" :type]]}
